# TARS architecture

> Naming: product = **TARS**. Older copies may say "Jarvis" — rename in copy
> when editing. Folder name `Jarvis/jarvis` stays for path stability.

## Stack

- Backend: Python, FastAPI-style. Routers in `web_extras/routers/`. Domain
  subsystems in `backend/core/*`. Agent entry points in `backend/agents/`.
- **Web UI:** the standalone React marketing/cockpit SPA was removed from this
  repo — **API-first**. The **desktop** app bundles static assets under
  `desktop/src-tauri/web/` (Tauri dev: `pnpm run serve:web` on port 5173).
- ⚠ Legacy `frontend/` (vanilla HTML/CSS/JS) was retired during the
  2026-05-02 system audit.

## Domain packs (Phase 9)

`backend/core/domains/` plugin system. Built-ins: `traders`, `business`,
`mlm`, `science`. Each pack:

- Manifest with slug, name, short, description, color, capabilities, audience.
- Async action handlers returning a dict with `ok`.
- Awareness sources of kind `stream` / `poll` / `webhook` / `local`.
- A constrained system prompt.

Router: `web_extras/routers/domains.py` (`/api/domains`). Spec:
`docs/DOMAIN_PACKS.md`. Tests: `tests/test_domains.py`,
`tests/test_meeet.py`.

## meeet.world bridge (Phase 9.1)

`backend/core/meeet/` adds end-to-end logging.

- `start_trace` / `current_trace` / `trace_scope` for context.
- `MeeetClient.emit(kind, payload)` (async, fire-and-forget) emits events to
  the meeet ingest endpoint with an `x-meeet-contract-version` header
  (default `1.0.0`).
- Env-driven: `MEEET_INGEST_URL`, `MEEET_API_KEY`, `MEEET_SOURCE`,
  `MEEET_CONTRACT_VERSION`, `MEEET_LOCAL_LOG`.
- Domain router accepts `x-meeet-trace-id` header to continue an upstream
  trace; emits `domain.action.invoked|completed|failed` per call.

## Frontend conventions

- New UIs consume `web_extras/routers/` or ship beside the desktop bundle.
- Follow `design-system/tars/MASTER.md` for visual baseline.
- Always provide empty / loading / error / success states.

## Backend conventions

- New endpoints in `web_extras/routers/`. Don't change response shapes
  silently; additive keys (`trace_id`, `took_ms`) are OK.
- Long-running work in `backend/core/background` with observability.

## Guardrails

- Scoped changes only.
- Never commit `.env`.
- Flag any cross-stack change.

## Design system

- Source of truth: `design-system/tars/MASTER.md`.
- Skill `nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill` installed in canonical
  agent paths:
  `~/.cursor/skills-cursor/ui-ux-pro-max/` (Cursor agent global),
  `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/` (Cursor project),
  `~/.claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/` (Claude Code global),
  `.claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/` (Claude Code project).
  Targeted lookups via `python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py
  "<query>" --domain <domain>`.
- Aesthetic blend (per MASTER): HUD/Sci-Fi FUI + Exaggerated Minimalism +
  Dark Mode (OLED) + AI-Native UI. One cyan accent (`#67E8F9`); amber
  (`#FBBF24`) reserved for live/alert telemetry.

